                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "48af9fc0-f09a-371e-b66d-1a59db656799",
                        "entry_id": "ff55ad82-f1d3-3d74-ab8f-ff75b0bdeb1f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "биохим. образование органических соединений живыми организмами"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c0aecc5-023d-40f6-b9fd-8524333d2286",
                                "sense_id": "48af9fc0-f09a-371e-b66d-1a59db656799",
                                "text": "На протяжении последних пятнадцати лет Бартон занимается химическим синтезом природных соединений и изучением путей их биогенеза, то есть их синтеза в природе."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1ef4f3a3-0436-49aa-a6f4-7286796d0769",
                        "source_entry_id": "ff55ad82-f1d3-3d74-ab8f-ff75b0bdeb1f",
                        "source_sense_id": "48af9fc0-f09a-371e-b66d-1a59db656799",
                        "target_lang_word": "biogenesis",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "biogenesis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c979a4fd-a3c4-334e-a7ee-bf629ea7a51a",
                                        "entry_id": "32718ab2-06b3-32eb-af56-4783f17c7538",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The principle that living organisms are produced only from other living organisms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6384b93f-d53c-4d9f-a8b4-31cec115148b",
                                                "sense_id": "c979a4fd-a3c4-334e-a7ee-bf629ea7a51a",
                                                "text": "And thus the hypothesis that living matter always arises by the agency of pre-existing living matter, took definite shape; […] It will be necessary for me to refer to this hypothesis so frequently, that, to save circumlocution, I shall call it the hypothesis of Biogenesis; and I shall term the contrary doctrine—that living matter may be produced by not living matter—the hypothesis of Abiogenesis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e0f51bb-8c82-480f-ba01-0c5cf9bf5659",
                                                "sense_id": "c979a4fd-a3c4-334e-a7ee-bf629ea7a51a",
                                                "text": "It is likely that the long evolutionary trajectory of Mycoplasma went from a reductive autotroph to oxidative heterotroph to a cell-wall–defective degenerate parasite. This evolutionary trajectory assumes the simplicity to complexity route of biogenesis, a point of view that is not universally accepted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22cc04ab-ee74-3142-9613-be6a90d91924",
                                        "entry_id": "32718ab2-06b3-32eb-af56-4783f17c7538",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Biosynthesis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
